{
  "version": 2,
  "updated": "2026-11-28",
  "about": "The meta-backend lane's service -> public API description map (meta/backend.mjs). One entry per hosted API a server's write tools can write to that publishes a machine-readable description writecheck's min mode can build a mock from. `signals` say how the lane recognises the service in a repository; `spec` is the description: an https URL, its format (openapi3, swagger2, google_discovery, smithy, graphql_sdl, graphql_introspection), who publishes it (vendor: the service's owner, in its own repository or domain) and when the URL was last read (checked). A subject is mock_min when its primary backend has a spec here and no usable stand-in in stand-ins.json. A known hosted API with no published description has spec null and a note saying when it was looked for: its servers are none, hosted_without_spec, reported as not testable, never as failures. Every URL was read on 27 Nov 2026 and answered with a description of that format. An id that is also in stand-ins.json is the same backend, merged. A spec URL is one API's description file: never a repository page or a directory of APIs; its path ends in .json, .yaml, .yml or .graphql, or `endpoint: true` says the URL itself serves the description. `objects`: the words a write tool uses for the service's objects; a server whose write tools name none of them is low confidence and not routed (R-WB-22). Add a service or move a URL here, not in code; meta/test/backend.test.mjs checks the shape. LLM providers, telemetry and error-reporting SDKs are left out on purpose: they are not where a server's write tools write.",
